{"chunk_id": "737190e552d1", "text": "Jarasandha defends his conduct before Krishna, declaring that he never imprisons a king without first defeating him in battle and that subjugating rivals is the duty of a Kshatriya. Refusing to release the captive monarchs he intends to sacrifice, he offers to fight any of the three visitors\u2014Krishna, Bhima, or Arjuna. Knowing Jarasandha is destined to die at Bhima\u2019s hands, Krishna lets Bhima accept the challenge. Jarasandha prepares ceremonially for combat and chooses Bhima as his opponent, acknowledging it is honorable to fall before a superior warrior. The two titans engage in a ferocious wrestling match before a massive crowd, using only their bodies as weapons. Their contest\u2014full of grappling holds, crushing blows, and earth\u2011shaking impacts\u2014unfolds like a clash of wild beasts, emphasizing both heroic strength and the warrior code that governs their actions.\nKrishna asks whom Jarasandha will fight; Jarasandha chooses Bhima, and the two begin a colossal bare\u2011handed wrestling duel before a vast crowd.\nThemes: heroic duel, kshatriya duty, wrestling combat, fate and destiny, public spectacle", "vector": [-0.007824202999472618, -0.0171482115983963, -0.004034873563796282, 0.01700221374630928, -0.0038291478995233774, 0.013551334850490093, -0.027009760960936546, -0.0006930790841579437, -0.013577879406511784, -0.010087183676660061, 0.008215744979679585, 0.004897593054920435, 0.0170818492770195, -0.0010435589356347919, -0.0008585719624534249, -0.0024322057142853737, 0.04000364616513252, -0.002691021654754877, 0.029013924300670624, -0.01724112033843994, -0.006855302955955267, -0.01717475615441799, -0.002445478457957506, 0.017440209165215492, -0.03644658625125885, 0.040879637002944946, 0.011573716066777706, -0.012316982261836529, 0.0027507483027875423, -0.017971113324165344, -0.012316982261836529, -0.004711776506155729, -0.0025201367679983377, 0.012443071231245995, -0.0255232285708189, 0.003563695820048451